    <h3>RNA-seq Aging Differential Expression - Young vs Old Human Brain</h3>
    <p>A bioinformatics pipeline that finds genes differentially expressed between young and old human cortex. Pulls the public GSE104704 cohort (8 young and 10 aged brains) as uniformly processed counts, runs DESeq2 with multiple-testing correction, and outputs an annotated results table plus PCA, volcano, and heatmap figures. Found 119 genes significant at 5 percent FDR, led by myelin, oligodendrocyte, and extracellular-matrix genes consistent with brain aging. Includes a self-diagnosing GEO loader that handles the inconsistent ways datasets store their counts.</p>
