    <h3>Clinical Readmission Risk Analysis</h3>
    <p>A 30-day hospital readmission risk analysis on a 300-patient clinical dataset, executed across R, SQL, Power BI, and Excel to show the same result holds across tools. The R logistic regression (glm) quantifies how each factor shifts the odds of readmission: relative to surgical patients, Heart Failure carries roughly 20x the odds (OR 19.7, p&lt;0.001), with COPD, Sepsis, and Pneumonia all 6-10x and significant, reported as odds ratios with 95% confidence intervals and ROC AUC 0.714.</p>
